    "teach_5": {
      "id": "teach_5",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "A conjugate product can remove a surd before the square root even starts.\n\n(7 + 3√5)(7 − 3√5)\n= 7² − (3√5)²",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_5_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_5_step": {
      "id": "teach_5_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "= 49 − 45 = 4\n\nSo:\n√[(7+3√5)(7−3√5)] = √4 = 2\n\nThe middle terms cancel because the signs are opposite.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
